# packages.optional.list - BAKED ONLY WHEN ASKED, INSTALLED BY NOTHING.
#
# WHAT THIS FILE IS. export-apt.sh resolves these names into the same baked repo
# as packages.list - but ONLY when BAKE_OPTIONAL=1, which this repo never sets.
# They are resolved in ONE closure with the core list, because two resolves can
# pick different versions of a shared dependency and the second would overwrite
# the first's deb in a flat repo. Late-command 3c installs only
# packages.baked.list, so nothing here is ever installed by an image, and
# late-command 3c-keep leaves /opt/homehub/apt registered as a `[trusted=yes]`
# apt source so these stay installable months later on a box that has never had
# internet.
#
# TWO DECISIONS, NOT ONE, AND THEY LIVE IN HOMEHUB. Whether these packages RIDE
# the USB is a BUILD decision; whether the box TURNS THEM ON is an INSTALL
# decision. Both are derived from one `Extras` declaration in HomeHub's
# scripts/deploy/config.homehub.psd1, and Materialize-Deploy refuses to emit an
# activation whose carriage is absent.
#
# THAT GATE IS THE POINT OF THE WHOLE ARRANGEMENT. Before it existed the two
# halves could disagree silently, and they did: the project told operators to
# "RDP in and sign in to IceDrive" for a month while ELEVEN of the AppImage's
# runtime libraries were in no image at all. The instruction could not have been
# followed on any hub this repo has ever built.
#
# FORMAT: identical to packages.list (read_packages_list): strip from `#` to end
# of line, strip all whitespace, drop what is left if empty.

# ── the RDP server and a MINIMAL XFCE session ───────────────────────────────
# --no-install-recommends applies here as everywhere, so this stays a window
# manager, a panel, a terminal and a file manager - not a desktop. Do not add
# xubuntu-desktop or the xfce4 meta-package.
xrdp                  # the RDP server itself
xorgxrdp              # the Xorg driver xrdp drives; without it sessions are black
dbus-x11              # dbus-launch - an XFCE session will not come up without it
xfce4-session         # the session manager ~/.xsession starts
xfwm4                 # window manager
xfce4-panel           # panel
xfce4-terminal        # a terminal inside the session
thunar                # file manager

# ── the unattended-session pair — RETIRED, and kept only to be installable ──
# These existed so a session could be created AT BOOT with nobody connected, to
# keep the GUI IceDrive client syncing (homehub-desktop-session.service). That
# unit is deleted: the CLI needs no session at all. They stay in the bake
# because setup-remote-ui.sh still refers to the mechanism for anyone who
# deliberately wants an unattended desktop for some FUTURE GUI-only app, and
# discovering the packages are missing at that point is the failure this file
# exists to prevent.
xvfb                  # scratch display for a loopback RDP client
freerdp2-x11          # xfreerdp: connects to loopback to make a session exist

# ── the IceDrive GUI AppImage's RUNTIME DEPENDENCIES ────────────────────────
# NOT OPTIONAL IF THE APPIMAGE IS CARRIED - the app does not start without every
# one of them. Measured on the bench box 2026-08-27 by installing it and
# following the failures one at a time, because each hides behind the one in
# front of it:
#
#   libwebpmux.so.3          the binary aborts before Qt starts
#   libwebpdemux.so.2         "
#   libXss.so.1               "
#   libxcb-icccm.so.4        "Could not load the Qt platform plugin xcb ...
#   libxcb-image.so.0         even though it was found", then a core dump.
#   libxcb-keysyms.so.1       Eight more, one per launch.
#   libxcb-render-util.so.0
#   libxcb-shape.so.0
#   libxcb-xinerama.so.0
#   libxcb-xkb.so.1
#   libxkbcommon-x11.so.0
#
# The AppImage bundles Qt but NOT the system libraries Qt's xcb platform plugin
# links against, and the failure names a PLUGIN rather than a PACKAGE - so it
# reads like a corrupt download and sent this project looking in the wrong place
# for a month.
libwebpmux3
libwebpdemux2
libxss1
libxcb-icccm4
libxcb-image0
libxcb-keysyms1
libxcb-render-util0
libxcb-shape0
libxcb-xinerama0
libxcb-xkb1
libxkbcommon-x11-0

# ── the FUSE 2 shim - needed by BOTH IceDrive builds ────────────────────────
# Ubuntu 24.04 ships libfuse3. The AppImage is built against FUSE 2 and exits
# with a libfuse.so.2 message that reads like a corrupt download; the CLI links
# it directly for its mount. Neither IceDrive build is present by default, so
# neither is this.
libfuse2t64
